## Summary
Authored one lesson at `courses/.../lessons/farmakoterapia-zasady-wyboru-leku-i-sekwencja-rzutow.json` — validates against `LessonSchema` (`OK`).
**Approach** — I grounded the content in the uploaded `syllabus-part3.txt` (Moduł 16) plus `research.md`/`sources.md`/`course.json`. The `research.md` "Notes for lesson generation" were decisive: this is an advanced medical course (`theoryPracticeRatio` 0.12), which explicitly bars `code`/`sandbox`/`demo`/`plotImage`/`histogram` widgets (no Python or numeric data) and recommends `theory` + `quiz` + `dragMatch` + `dataTable`. No external images were needed, so no asset caching/materialization step applied.
**Structure** (9 sections — 4 theory beats, 5 widgets, no back-to-back theory, ends on a widget):
1. Theory — five elements of treatment, ASM nomenclature, decision to treat (recurrence-risk table 44/32/17%, prevention syndromes incl. TSC/EPISTOP)
2. Quiz (single) — applying recurrence risk factors
3. Theory — 7 drug-selection criteria, generations, START LOW GO SLOW titration (NICE source)
4. DataTable — AAN infant first-line vs drug-resistant recommendations
5. DragMatch — slow vs fast titration drugs (multi-item zones)
6. Theory — drugs that worsen generalized seizures + PTN 2022 sex-based JME choice, with corrective blockquotes (NICE source)
7. Quiz (multi) — which drugs to avoid in JME
