## Prerequisite Order

- The 5-minute T1 threshold for status epilepticus is used in `drgawki-goraczkowe` before it is defined. That lesson's quiz explanation states "o stanie padaczkowym mówimy dopiero od 5 min utrzymującego się napadu," yet the operational T1/T2 definition is only introduced in the next lesson of the same module, `stan-padaczkowy`. Either move a one-line definition into `drgawki-goraczkowe` or add a forward-pointer ("zdefiniujemy w lekcji o stanie padaczkowym").

- `emats-fires-i-inne-dee` relies on **niedrgawkowy stan padaczkowy (NCSE)** ("u <50% pojawia się NCSE") and on the **dieta ketogenna** as named treatments, but both are only formally introduced later — NCSE (the >2,5 Hz EEG criterion) in `stan-padaczkowy` (m4) and the ketogenic diet (mechanism, types, contraindications, propofol pitfall) in `leczenie-niefarmakologiczne-dieta-keto-vns-cbd-mtor` (m6). The same forward dependency on the ketogenic diet runs through `zespo-westa`, `choroby-metaboliczne-zwiazane-z-padaczka-i-deficyt-glut1`, and `padaczki-uogolnione-wieku-dzieciecego`. Each early mention is locally functional ("leczenie z wyboru w GLUT1"), so this is a soft ordering issue, but a forward-pointer to the m6 lesson would help.

- The formal ILAE definition of drug resistance (failure of two properly-chosen, tolerated regimens; Kwan 2010) appears only in `farmakoterapia-zasady-wyboru-leku-i-sekwencja-rzutow` (m6), while "lekooporność/lekooporna" is used as a load-bearing term from `wprowadzenie-definicje-ilae-epidemiologia-etiologia-i-patofizjologia` (m1, informal "~30%") onward through the Dravet, LGS, FIRES, and metabolic lessons. This is acceptable pedagogically (loose concept early, formalized in the treatment module) but worth a forward-pointer at first substantive use.

## Redundancy

- `diagnostyka-eeg-i-wideo-eeg` and `zespo-westa-i-napady-zgieciowe` both define the three-element hipsarytmia (chaotyczne tło delta + wieloogniskowe wyładowania z ≥2–3 ognisk + asynchronia międzypółkulowa) from scratch, with the same "non-REM, znika w REM, wrzeciona snu nie dyskwalifikują" qualifiers and neither acknowledging the other. Make `diagnostyka-eeg-i-wideo-eeg` the canonical definition and have `zespo-westa-i-napady-zgieciowe` recap it ("przypomnij z lekcji o EEG…").

- `emats-fires-i-inne-dee` and `zespo-rasmussena-fires-i-norse` independently teach the full FIRES picture — febrile infection 24 h–2 tyg. prior, IL-1/IL-6 in PMR, bilateral temporal+insula+thalamus MRI, anakinra as first choice within ~2 weeks, ~10% mortality, and the "FIRES = NORSE u dziecka" relationship. The m5 lesson legitimately adds the Rasmussen contrast, but the clinical FIRES block is duplicated without cross-reference; the second occurrence should cite the first and keep only the comparative material.

- The genotype-driven gene→therapy content is largely duplicated between `genetyka-padaczek` (section "geny-i-terapia-celowana") and `korelacje-genotyp-fenotyp-kazuistyka-kliniczna`: both teach SCN1A LoF→avoid Na-blockers vs GoF→use them, KCNQ2 frameshift-benign vs missens-encephalopathy→carbamazepine, GRIN2A LoF→memantyna / GoF→radiprodyl, and CDKL5→ganaksolon. The m7 lesson adds the case studies (Iwonka, Zosia) and more genes, but re-derives the shared table; it should reference `genetyka-padaczek` rather than restate it.

- The prophylactic-vigabatrin-in-TSC story (EPISTOP/VIRAP, "jedyny w padaczce przykład", monitorowanie pola widzenia) is told in full in `zespo-westa-i-napady-zgieciowe`, again in full in `stwardnienie-guzowate-tsc`, and a third time in `farmakoterapia-zasady-wyboru-leku-i-sekwencja-rzutow`, with no cross-reference between them. One canonical treatment (the TSC lesson) and short recaps elsewhere would remove the repetition. (The parallel passages in the `pytania-kontrolne-*` lessons are explicit module recaps and are not counted here.)

## Notation Consistency

- Valproate is named three different ways across (and sometimes within) lessons: **kwas walproinowy**, **walproinian**, and **walproat**. `encefalopatie-padaczkowo-rozwojowe-zespo-dravet-i-lgs` alone uses all three ("kwas walproinowy (I rzut)", "redukcją/odstawieniem walproatu", "ostrożnie z walproinianem"), while other lessons settle variably on "walproinian" (`padaczki-modziencze-i-ogniskowe-rodzinne`) or "kwas walproinowy". Pick one primary term and use it consistently.

- The diagnostic GLUT1 cutoff (stosunek glukozy PMR/surowica) is given with inconsistent numbers across lessons: "<0,6" in `emats-fires-i-inne-dee`, "0,41–0,51 (norma ok. 0,65)" in `choroby-metaboliczne-zwiazane-z-padaczka-i-deficyt-glut1`, "<0,5–0,6" in `pytania-kontrolne-zespoy-wieku-niemowlecego`, and "<0,5" in `pytania-kontrolne-stany-metaboliczne-i-nage` and `aneks-skroty-akronimy-programy-lekowe-nfz-i-osrodki-referencyjne`. A learner comparing lessons sees the same threshold as both "<0,6" and "<0,5"; standardize the stated cutoff.

- The abbreviation for a generalized tonic-clonic seizure drifts between **GTCS** (`padaczki-modziencze-i-ogniskowe-rodzinne`) and **GTC** (`pytania-kontrolne-egzamin-podsumowujacy-pes`), separate from the syndrome abbreviation **GTCA**. Minor, but worth fixing one of the two seizure abbreviations so GTCA isn't visually confused with GTC/GTCS.
